            <div xml:id="d1045">

                <pb facs="0924" n="917" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg917"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/8585: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of Embassy in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lockhart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-19T11:00:00+08:00">April 19, 1937—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 19—12:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>124. The following message has been received from Mukden: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 17, 11 a.m. My despatch No. 16 [<hi rendition="#italic">96</hi>],
                            March 19th. Information contained in second and third paragraphs is
                            verified by authoritative French military source which adds that Second
                            and Fourth Divisions are being sent from Japan to Manchuria not as
                            replacements.</p>
                        <p>Repeated to Tokyo.[”]</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lockhart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
